      "table_no": null,
      "title": "[Units of the National Research Institute completely organized in 1927-1928]",
      "caption_extra": "\"In 1927-1928, we find the following units completely organized :\"",
      "continued": false,
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": null,
          "columns": [
            "No.",
            "Unit",
            "Description"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "(1)",
              "Departments of Astronomy and of Meteorology",
              "This unit is in Nanking. Two most picturesque spots are utilised for observational and experimental purposes, the little hill called Pei on Pei Chi Ko."
            ],
            [
              "(2)",
              "Departments of Physics, Chemistry, and of Engineering",
              "These departments are grouped in one building with well-equipped laboratories, now erected on Avenue Joffre, Shanghai."
            ],
            [
              "(3)",
              "Department of Social Sciences",
              "Located at Paotung Road, Shanghai."
            ],
            [
              "(4)",
              "Department of History and Language",
              "This department is attached to the Chung Shan University, Canton."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        "The total expenditure for the maintenance of the various units this year is $600,000. Dr. Tsai is the general Director of the Institute."
      ],
      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Numbered run-in paragraphs; unit name printed as a run-in heading followed by an em dash."
